  margin-bottom: .001pt;\r\n}\r\n</style><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"SD 23A-19 - THE JURY PANEL\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"SDLRC Codified Law 23A-19 - THE JURY PANEL\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes?Statute=23A-19\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lawmakerdocuments.blob.core.usgovcloudapi.net/photos/logoshape.webp\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"South Dakota Legislature\"></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622HG4\">CHAPTER </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19</span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622HG4C\">THE JURY PANEL </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622Normal-000000\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-1\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-1</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Panel defined. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-2\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-2</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Challenge to panel defined. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-3\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-3</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Grounds for challenge to panel--Bias of officer summoning additional jurors.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-4\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-4</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Time for challenge to panel--Ground stated. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-5\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-5</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Challenge to panel when several defendants tried together. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-6\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-6</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Objection to challenge--Entry and trial. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-7\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-7</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Trial of sufficiency of challenge--Trial of fact issues. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-8\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-8</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Examination of officers on trial of challenge to panel. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-9\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-9</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    New jury on allowance of challenge to panel--Jury impaneled if challenge disallowed. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-10\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-10</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Calling of jurors' names when case ready for trial--Attachment for absent jurors. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-11\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-11</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    Drawing of names of jurors. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2083622B\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-12\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-12</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">    </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-12\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-19-12</span></a><span class=\"s2083622DefaultParagraphFont\"><span>. Repealed by <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><span><a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\">SL 2003, ch 115</a></span></a></span></a></span></a></span></a></span></a></span></a>, § 4</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048627Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048627Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048627SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048627Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-1\"><span class=\"s2048627SENU\">23A-19-1</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048627SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048627CL\">Panel defined.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048627Normal-000000\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048627DefaultParagraphFont\">A panel is a list of jurors drawn pursuant to chapter </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=16-13\"><span class=\"s2048627DefaultParagraphFont\">16-13</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048627DefaultParagraphFont\"> to serve at a particular court or for the trial of a particular action.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048627Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048627000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048627Normal\"><span class=\"s2048627SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048627SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3610; SDCL, § 23-43-9; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 262.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048628Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048628Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048628SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048628Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-2\"><span class=\"s2048628SENU\">23A-19-2</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048628SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048628CL\">Challenge to panel defined.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048628Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048628DefaultParagraphFont\">A challenge to a panel is an objection made to all the trial jurors drawn, and may be taken by either party.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048628Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048628000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048628Normal\"><span class=\"s2048628SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048628SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3610; SDCL, § 23-43-10; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 263.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en-US\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2082641Normal {\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: .001pt;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2082641Statute {\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: .001pt;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641000000 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2082641NoIndent {\r\n    text-indent: 0.00in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: .001pt;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641DefaultParagraphFont-000001 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2082641SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"SD 23A-19-3 - Grounds for challenge to panel--Bias of officer summoning additional jurors.\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"SDLRC Codified Law 23A-19-3 - Grounds for challenge to panel--Bias of officer summoning additional jurors.\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes?Statute=23A-19-3\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lawmakerdocuments.blob.core.usgovcloudapi.net/photos/logoshape.webp\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"South Dakota Legislature\"></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2082641Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-3\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2082641SENU\">23A-19-3</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641SENU\">. </span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641CL\">Grounds for challenge to panel--Bias of officer summoning additional jurors. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2082641Statute\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont\">A challenge to a panel may only be based on a material departure from the procedure prescribed by law for the drawing and return of the jury, or on the intentional omission of the board of jury selectors or sheriff to summon one or more of the jurors drawn. However, if the panel is composed of any persons who were summoned to serve as jurors pursuant to § </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=16-13-42\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont\">16-13-42</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont\">, a challenge may be taken to the panel based upon the alleged bias of the officer who summoned them if such bias would be sufficient grounds for a challenge to an individual juror under § </span><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-20-13.1\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont\">23A-20-13.1</span></a><span class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont\">. Such challenge must be determined in the same manner as if made to an individual juror for bias.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2082641Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641000000\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2082641NoIndent\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2082641DefaultParagraphFont-000001\">Source:  </span><span class=\"s2082641SCL\"><span>SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, §§ 34.3611, 34.3612; SDCL, §§ 23-43-11, 23-43-14; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 264; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2021/86/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2021, ch 86\">SL 2021, ch 86</a>, § 4.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048630Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048630Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048630SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048630Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-4\"><span class=\"s2048630SENU\">23A-19-4</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048630SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048630CL\">Time for challenge to panel--Ground stated.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048630Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048630DefaultParagraphFont\">A challenge to a panel must be taken before a juror is sworn, and must be in writing, specifying plainly and distinctly the facts constituting the ground of challenge.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048630Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048630000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048630Normal\"><span class=\"s2048630SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048630SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3611; SDCL, § 23-43-12; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 265.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048631Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048631Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048631SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048631Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-5\"><span class=\"s2048631SENU\">23A-19-5</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048631SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048631CL\">Challenge to panel when several defendants tried together.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048631Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048631DefaultParagraphFont\">When several defendants are tried together, any individual defendant may challenge the panel, but if more than one defendant challenges the panel, the challenges must be tried together.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048631Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048631000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048631Normal\"><span class=\"s2048631SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048631SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3611; SDCL, § 23-43-13; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 266.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048632Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048632Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048632SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048632Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-6\"><span class=\"s2048632SENU\">23A-19-6</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048632SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048632CL\">Objection to challenge--Entry and trial.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048632Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048632DefaultParagraphFont\">An objection to a challenge need not be in writing, but must be entered upon the court minutes and thereupon the court must try the challenge.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048632Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048632000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048632Normal\"><span class=\"s2048632SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048632SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3613; SDCL, § 23-43-15; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 267.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048633Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048633Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048633SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048633Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-7\"><span class=\"s2048633SENU\">23A-19-7</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048633SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048633CL\">Trial of sufficiency of challenge--Trial of fact issues.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048633Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048633DefaultParagraphFont\">A court must first try the sufficiency of a challenge, assuming the facts alleged therein to be true. If the court determines that the facts alleged, if true, constitute sufficient grounds for challenge to the panel, the objecting party may then deny the facts alleged in the challenge. The denial may be oral and must be entered on the record. The court must then proceed to try the issue of fact.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048633Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048633000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048633Normal\"><span class=\"s2048633SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048633SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3613; SDCL, §§ 23-43-15, 23-43-16; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 268.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048634Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048634Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048634SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048634Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-8\"><span class=\"s2048634SENU\">23A-19-8</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048634SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048634CL\">Examination of officers on trial of challenge to panel.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048634Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048634DefaultParagraphFont\">Upon the trial of a challenge to the panel, the officers, whether judicial or ministerial, whose irregularity is complained of, as well as any other persons, may be examined to prove or disprove the facts alleged as the ground of the challenge.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048634Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048634000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048634Normal\"><span class=\"s2048634SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048634SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3613; SDCL, § 23-43-18; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 269.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048635Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048635Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048635SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048635Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-9\"><span class=\"s2048635SENU\">23A-19-9</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048635SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048635CL\">New jury on allowance of challenge to panel--Jury impaneled if challenge disallowed.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048635Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048635DefaultParagraphFont\">If a challenge to a panel is allowed, the judge shall order a jury to be drawn and summoned in the regular manner. If it is disallowed, the court must direct the jury to be impaneled.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048635Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048635000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048635Normal\"><span class=\"s2048635SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048635SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3614; SDCL, § 23-43-19; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 270.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048636Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048636Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048636SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048636Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-10\"><span class=\"s2048636SENU\">23A-19-10</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048636SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048636CL\">Calling of jurors' names when case ready for trial--Attachment for absent jurors.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048636Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048636DefaultParagraphFont\">When a case is called for trial, and before drawing the jury, either party may require the names of all the jurors in the panel to be called, and the court in its discretion may order that an attachment issue against those who are absent; but the court may, in its discretion, wait for the return of the attachment.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048636Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048636000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048636Normal\"><span class=\"s2048636SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048636SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3604; SDCL, § 23-43-2; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 271.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048637Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048637Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048637Normal-000001 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.25in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637000002 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048637SCL-000003 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048637Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-19-11\"><span class=\"s2048637SENU\">23A-19-11</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048637SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048637CL\">Drawing of names of jurors.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048637Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048637DefaultParagraphFont\">At the opening of court the clerk shall randomly draw the names of the persons summoned as jurors by an electronic process or prepare separate ballots, containing the names of the persons summoned as jurors and deposit the ballots in a suitable container.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048637Normal-000001\"><span class=\"s2048637DefaultParagraphFont\">If an electronic process is not used, the clerk shall, under the direction of the court, publicly draw out of the container the appropriate number of ballots to form the jury. Before the name of any juror is drawn, the container shall be closed and the contents shall be intermingled. The clerk shall then, without looking at the ballots, draw them from the container.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048637Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048637000002\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048637Normal\"><span class=\"s2048637SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048637SCL-000003\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, §§ 34.3605, 34.3606; SDCL, §§ 23-43-5, 23-43-6; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 272; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\">SL 2003, ch 115</a>, § 3.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br>                                                                   \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<title>23A-19-12 </title>\r\n<meta name=\"Keywords\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws SDCL 23A-19-12 \">\r\n<meta name=\"Description\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws 23A-19-12\">\r\n</head>\r\n<body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\">\r\n\r\n<!-- File converted by Wp2Html Version 4.0  -->\r\n<!-- Email Andrew@brackenbeds.co.uk for more details  -->\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: System_34 --><!-- WP Style End: System_34 -->\r\n<div align=\"full\">\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: SENU -->    <!-- WP Style End: SENU -->\r\n23A-19-12.\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: SENU --> <!-- WP Style End: SENU -->\r\nRepealed by <a rel=\"noopener\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\"><a rel=\"noopener\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/2003/115/null\" aria-label=\"SL 2003, ch 115\">SL 2003, ch 115</a></a>, &#167; 4<p>\r\n</p></div></div></body>\r\n</html>\r\n</head></html>","Credits":null,"StatuteText":null,"Article":null,"Created":null,"CreatedById":null,"LastUpdated":null,"LastUpdatedBy":null,"Repealed":false,"StatuteReferencesReferencesStatute":[],"StatuteReferencesStatute":[]}